{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-400499-r4518452","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Mohingha (Burmese Fish Noodle Soup)","sourcePageId":400499,"sourceRevision":"4518452","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T16:27:32Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Mohingha%20(Burmese%20Fish%20Noodle%20Soup)&oldid=4518452","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:09:19.205Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Burmese recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for soup","Category:Recipes using jalapeño chile","Category:Recipes using ketchup","Category:Recipes using sunflower oil","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"5e0bc55efce3f11fd8eb0b5976ea9b5b8fc4f5acdb183a08798ac33dea76191d","sourceWikitext":"{{recipe summary\n| category = Soup recipes\n| servings = 4\n| time = 20 minutes\n| difficulty = 1\n| image = \n| energy = \n| note = \n}}{{Recipe}}\n\n'''Mohingha''' is a traditional Burmese dish made of colored [[Cookbook:Soup|soup]] with rice vermicelli. Here is a modern-day recipe. It is recommended that you top your mohingha with [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]] slices and Naga viper [[Cookbook:Chiles|peppers]]; however, the use of [[Cookbook:Tabasco Sauce|Tabasco]] habanero [[Cookbook:Hot Sauce|Pepper sauce]], fish fingers, and [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]] is also acceptable.\n[[File:Mohinga.jpg|alt=Mohingha soup powder|thumb|Mohingha soup powder]]\n\n==Ingredients==\n*5 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Sunflower Oil|sunflower oil]]\n*10 [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]] cloves\n*30 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]] [[Cookbook:Lemonade|lemonade]]\n*70 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] Mohingha soup powder\n*⅞ [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Boiling|boiling]] water\n*100 g [[Cookbook:Jalapeño|jalapeno peppers]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Ketchup|ketchup]]\n*60 g instant rice [[Cookbook:Vermicelli|vermicelli]]\n\n==Instructions==\n#In a large bowl, mix sunflower oil, garlic cloves, soup powder, and lemonade for 3 minutes.\n#In a small bowl, mix boiling water, diced jalapeño peppers, and ketchup for 5 minutes.\n#Combine both mixtures, and continue mixing for 2 ½ minutes.\n#Add rice vermicelli to the bowl; cover it and wait for 10 minutes.\n#Top it with toppings as desired.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for soup]]\n[[Category:Burmese recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sunflower oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using jalapeño chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ketchup]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Mohingha (Burmese Fish Noodle Soup)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"4","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"5 tsp sunflower oil","sourceText":"5 tsp sunflower oil","amountText":"5 tsp sunflower oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"10 garlic cloves","sourceText":"10 garlic cloves","amountText":"10 garlic cloves","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"30 ml lemonade","sourceText":"30 ml lemonade","amountText":"30 ml lemonade","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"70 g Mohingha soup powder","sourceText":"70 g Mohingha soup powder","amountText":"70 g Mohingha soup powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBind